## Interface: 30300
## Title: COA Dungeon Run
## Notes: v0.15.1 - capture, display and CURATION. A dungeon route IS a sequence of pulls, so record the pulls: combat start and end are the markers, the path between them is sampled once a second out of combat, and both entrances are captured automatically. Records everything and filters nothing - judgement happens offline against the whole set. Also records the instance identity and DIFFICULTY at arrival, which bosses the route ENGAGED (never a roster, never a fraction), and who killed you at a terminal stop - read from the client's own DeathRecap rather than a second combat-log listener. The map draws a run back onto the client's own tiles and never learns a dungeon; point facts live on the MAP as a tooltip; the companion is the CURATION pane - load, rename, comment, delete, filter by kind, and slice by TIME with an envelope, a window, play and skip. Curation only ever changes what you SEE: nothing it does touches the record. Also a CUSTOM PIN: where the client emits no event, the player is the sensor - /dr pin drops a point and promotion gives it meaning later. The map now holds LAYERS rather than a run - a run slot and a route slot, loaded independently - because authoring a route means looking at the evidence it came from. And PROMOTION is the third surface: select a node, mint a beacon into a route or a personal note onto your own plane - place carries over, the event does not, and the meaning is edited in afterwards. /dr
